WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.669
-The one-year anniversary of
President Trump's inauguration

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.705
was marked this weekend
by nationwide protests

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.374
and a government shutdown
that ended today

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:11.044
despite Trump doing as little
as possible it resolve it.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.913
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.349 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.318 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.687
It's been a year since
Trump's inauguration

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.655
and the historic
women's marches that followed.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:25.792
And on Saturday, we saw yet
again that the women's march

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.193
wasn't merely
a one-time phenomenon,

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.728
but a sustained movement

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.597
unlike anything the country's
seen in decades.

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.532
-Women across the country were
on the march today.

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.436
Thousands took to the streets
from coast to coast.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.804
They rallied for a variety
of causes with a focus

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:43.042
on having their voices heard
in November's midterm elections.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:47.379
-Taking to the streets in over
300 rallies in all 50 states.

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:50.283
-But it just wasn't in the U.S.
where women marched.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.286
This was the scene in
Nova Scotia, where half the town

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:57.624
of Sandy Cove also participated
in the women's march.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:01.894
-Wow.
Half the town was protesting.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.564
That, I have to say...

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.165
[ Applause ]

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.968
That's got to be super awkward
for people who weren't there.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.236
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.238
"Dale, I didn't see you
at the women's march."

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.507
"Oh, yeah,
was it a good turnout?"

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.944
"Half, Dale! It was half."

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.479
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.681
Of course, one of the best parts
of any protests are the signs,

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.249
and this year was especially
refreshing

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.418
to see children participating,

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.486
like this sign
that said "Vote for women!"

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:28.921
This sign that said

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.390
"boys are equal to girls
and girls are equal to boys,"

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.492
and then there was
this little girl

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.193
who clearly got
to write her own sign.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.694
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:38.497
Although...
[ Applause ]

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:41.233
To be fair, it's possible
she spent more time on that

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.803
than the Trump administration
did on the original travel ban.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.438
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.873
[ Imitating Trump ]
"Don't forget.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:50.576
"Don't forget
the purple circles.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:53.079
The purple circles make it
legally airtight."

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:55.815
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.650
Of course, Trump, who was cooped
up in the White House

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.485
all weekend watching coverage
of the protests,

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.355
couldn't help but weigh in,
tweeting...

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.136
Dude, you know that's not why
they were marching.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.737
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:22.241
Trump's the kind of guy, who if
he came home to find his wife

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:25.712
dumped all his clothes on
the sidewalk, would say to her,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.946
"I get it.
You want to see me naked."

00:02:27.946 --> 00:02:30.182
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:34.120
"I pick up on stuff.
I pick up on stuff."

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.054
[ Applause ]

00:02:36.054 --> 00:02:37.924
So the one-year anniversary
of Trump's inauguration

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:40.827
saw a second straight year of
sustained nationwide protests

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.062
but, of course, it wasn't just
the protests

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.331
that marred Trump's celebration.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.532
-The government is shut down

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:49.001
for the first time
in more than four years.

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:52.238
"The Art of the Deal" President
could not reach that deal

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.839
with Democrats
and a few Republicans,

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:56.776
and just a few hours ago, they
marked the one-year anniversary

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.946
of his presidency
by rejecting a budget bill.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.048
-This is the first time
in modern history,

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.383
the first time
in modern U.S. history,

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:05.952
that a party that's controlled

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:08.253
the House, the Senate,
and the White House,

00:03:08.253 --> 00:03:11.390
has had a government shutdown
on their watch.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.825
-You got to hand it to Trump,

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.761
he finally did something no
other President has ever done.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.364
[ Imitating Trump ] "Bush
couldn't do it, Obama couldn't.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.200
We made history.
We made history."

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.602
Now Trump has, of course, tried
to claim it's actually Democrats

00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:25.438
who will suffer politically
from the shutdown,

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.640
tweeting over the weekend...

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:35.882
But there's at least one
immutable law of physics

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.383
that still applies
in Washington.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:41.921
For each Trump quote, there's an
equal and opposite Trump quote.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.257
And the question of who's to
blame for government shutdowns

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:47.326
is no exception because when
Obama was President,

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:50.429
Trump was very clear about
who was to blame.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:51.831
-Who's going to bear the brunt
of the responsibility

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:54.433
if, indeed, there is a shutdown
of our government?

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:56.268
-Well, if you say,
"who gets fired?" it always has

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:59.172
to be the top. I mean,
problems start from the top,

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.773
and have to get solved
from the top,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.242
and the President's the leader.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:07.179
In 25 years, in 50 years,
in a hundred years from now,

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:10.016
when the government is,
you know, they talk

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.485
about the government shutdown,
they're going to be talking

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:13.953
about the President
of the United States.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.955
Who was the President
at that time?

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.457
If there is a shutdown,
I think it would be

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.592
a tremendously negative mark

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.828
on the President
of the United States.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.028
I hear the Democrats are going
to be blamed

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.764
and the Republicans
are going to be blamed.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.500
I actually think the President
would be blamed.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.303
-There's literally, literally...

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:35.241
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:38.577
...not one situation where there
isn't an old Trump quote

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:41.280
that completely contradicts
his current position.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.249
I wouldn't be surprised if
there's an old Trump tweet

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.851
out there that says,
"Only a loser

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.986
would wear a baseball cap
with a suit."

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.621
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.923
In fact, Trump was asked
point-blank in 2011 how he would

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.092
handle a potential shutdown
differently

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.527
from then-President Obama.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:58.097
And in retrospect, let's say
he was a little overconfident.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.998
-I'm a deal man. I made hundreds
and hundreds of deals

00:04:59.998 --> 00:05:02.402
and transactions.
He never did deals before.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.937
How can you expect a man
that's not a deal man

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.740
that never did a deal
other than, frankly,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.775
becoming President
of the United States,

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.076
he never did a deal --

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:12.912
how is he going to corral all
these people?

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.014
-So how would you do it now?
Now you're in the Oval Office

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.783
right now, it's Wednesday --
-I would get everybody together

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:20.453
and we'd have a budget.
-They've all gotten together.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.523
-Well, that's because they
don't have the right leader.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.957
You don't have the right leader.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.326
This is the President
of the United States

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.362
has to get this done,
but it's pretty sad

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.530
because the whole world
is looking at us

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.633
and laughing at us.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.668
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:37.036
-It's amazing.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.137
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:41.941
I agree with everything
he just said.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.409
Of course, in reality,
Republicans control

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.344
all three branches of government
and on top of that,

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.980
we have a President
who repeatedly sold himself

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.716
on the campaign trail
as an ultimate dealmaker.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:54.319
-We need a President that's
going to be able to make deals,

00:05:54.319 --> 00:05:56.755
great deals.
I want to make great deals.

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:58.357
That's what it is.
For the people.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:01.761
I do hundreds of deals.
The deals come out of my ears.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:05.398
If you can't make a good deal
with a politician,

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.698
then there's
something wrong you.

00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:08.534
You're certainly not very good.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.137
You can't leave the White House,
go to Hawaii and play golf

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.071
for three weeks
and be a real dealmaker.

00:06:13.071 --> 00:06:14.807
It doesn't work that way.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.109
-That's right. You can't go
to Hawaii to play golf

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:19.812
and be a dealmaker.
You have to go to Florida.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.313
And you can't do it
for three weeks.

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:24.216
You have to do it
for an entire year.

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:25.984
And yet even as the government
shutdown ended,

00:06:25.984 --> 00:06:27.820
the self-proclaimed deal man
was M.I.A.,

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.621
completely absent
from the negotiations

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:32.090
and leaving everyone confused
about where he stood.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.960
In fact, in order to counter
that growing impression

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.896
that Trump was sitting around
doing nothing,

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.499
the White House released
a series of official photos

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.600
of what they called
President Donald J. Trump

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.403
working in the White House
during the Democrat shutdown,

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:46.405
including this photo of Trump
walking around,

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:48.774
this photo of Trump talking
to people,

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.410
and this photo of Trump
supposedly on the phone.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.979
Look at him. [ Imitating Trump ]
"Hello, police, come quick.

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:56.582
Somebody stole
all the work off my desk."

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.050
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.685
You know, you don't really look
like you're working

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:02.020
when you're staring directly
at the camera.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.891
You look like you just got
busted having phone sex.

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:11.697
[ Imitating Trump ] "I got to...
call you back."

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:16.569
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.104
The main reason the government
was in this mess

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:21.240
in the first place
was that Trump doesn't know

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.376
what he believes other
than the fact that he spent

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:25.344
the entire campaign promising
to build a wall,

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:28.280
and now his party's scrambling
to find a way to follow through

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.949
on that promise even though
they know it's absurd.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:32.584
Even Trump's Chief of Staff,
John Kelly,

00:07:32.584 --> 00:07:35.454
reportedly told lawmakers
Trump's promises on the wall

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:38.256
were uninformed and is now
saying the so-called wall

00:07:38.256 --> 00:07:42.027
doesn't even have to be
an actual physical barrier.

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:45.597
-Did he really say the President
was uninformed on the wall?

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:49.201
-Yes. Well, I had a meeting.
I was sitting right next to him,

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:52.037
next to Mr. Kelly,
and here's what he said.

00:07:52.037 --> 00:07:54.407
He said, "the President
of the United States,

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:58.210
"when he was campaigning,
made promises

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.013
that were not fully informed."

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.415
He said "I've educated
the President,

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:06.118
and the President
has evolved on the issue."

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.387
And when I asked General Kelly
"what's a wall?"

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:11.490
he said it could be
the inhospitable terrain,

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.626
it could be border patrol agent,
it could be drones.

00:08:14.626 --> 00:08:17.195
-Oh, my God, this wall
keeps getting worse and worse.

00:08:17.195 --> 00:08:19.064
It could be terrain,
it could be drones.

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:20.232
Soon, it's just going to be
a tunnel

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:22.201
painted on the side
of a mountain.

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:23.669
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:26.806
So we have a President making
cartoonish demands

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:28.407
that everyone
knows are impractical.

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:30.109
There's absolutely
no guiding principles

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:33.512
or knowledge of policy, and he
changes his views on a whim

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.113
depending on who
he's talking to.

00:08:35.113 --> 00:08:37.149
And a former campaign aide told
"The New York Times"

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:39.519
that Trump
doesn't even care to learn...

00:08:49.995 --> 00:08:51.730
So it's simple.
It's not that he does not know

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.599
what he does not know,
it's that he does know

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.801
what he does not know,
which means he doesn't know

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.836
what he does know
and he does think

00:08:57.836 --> 00:09:01.106
that he doesn't need to know it.
You know?

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:04.477
[ Cheers and applause ]
Just to give you...

00:09:04.477 --> 00:09:06.778
[ Applause ]

00:09:06.778 --> 00:09:08.480
Just to give you an idea
of how incoherent

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.016
and scattershot Trump's views
are, he spent the weekend

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:14.086
bashing Democrats over DACA,
tweeting...

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:19.925
Even though he, himself,
has spent months insisting

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:21.727
that he wants to deal
with the DREAMers,

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.562
the young undocumented
immigrants

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:26.432
brought here as children,
with compassion.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:30.169
-The DACA situation is a very,
very -- it's a very difficult

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:34.005
thing for me because, you know,
I love these kids.

00:09:34.005 --> 00:09:36.741
I love kids. I have kids.

00:09:36.741 --> 00:09:39.044
They shouldn't be very worried.
They are here illegally.

00:09:39.044 --> 00:09:41.813
They shouldn't be very worried.
I do have a big heart.

00:09:41.813 --> 00:09:43.816
We're going to take care
of everybody.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:46.751
Well, I have a great heart for
the folks we're talking about.

00:09:46.751 --> 00:09:49.522
A great love for them.

00:09:49.522 --> 00:09:53.558
I feel having the Democrats
in with us is absolutely vital

00:09:53.558 --> 00:09:55.061
because this should be
a bipartisan deal.

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:59.665
This should be a bill of love,
truly, should be a bill of love.

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:02.234
-Of course, a bill of love
is also what Trump pays

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:04.103
porn stars in hush money.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:06.038
[ Rimshot ]

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:12.845
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:12.845 --> 00:10:15.046
This weekend's shutdown was
very much the Trump presidency,

00:10:15.046 --> 00:10:17.349
a microcosm, the President
with no guiding principles

00:10:17.349 --> 00:10:19.518
and no knowledge of policy,
flailing wildly,

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.420
and relegated to making
cartoonish demands

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.589
from the sidelines while
everyone else scrambles

00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:25.390
to figure out how
to make it work.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.393
I don't know what Trump would
say about that,

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:30.429
but I do know how
his biggest critic feels.

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:33.933
-The whole world is looking
at us and laughing at us.

00:10:33.933 --> 00:10:36.335
-He's right.
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:36.335 --> 00:10:38.470 line:0%
♪♪

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.939 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

